id: pm-gantt-chart-observed-duration
title: Calibrate future task durations from verified observed episodes
description: Compare planned effort at verified start with elapsed completion history for an explicitly selected task class; return an empirical sampled distribution without replacing estimates.
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: calibration,scheduling
created_at: "2026-10-25T06:29:04.581Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T14:49:39.780Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Canceled, reopened and incomplete histories are disclosed; fewer than the declared sample minimum refuses calibration; a fixed corpus yields reproducible quantiles and sample counts."
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T06:29:08.387Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: CLI source has no observed task-duration calibration; its calibration APIs concern emitted-byte budgets. Existing gantt uncertainty consumes declared point/uniform/triangular effort; pm-brief summarizeMomentum reports throughput and closed_at cycle-time summaries. This feature reads verified lifecycle episodes and compares elapsed calendar minutes with planned minutes at start. It supplies explicit empirical scenario inputs, makes no causal productivity claim, and never replaces estimates. New command has no import, sync, journal, claim, outbox or mutation path; existing export remains read-only. Model-based tests will exercise seeded SDK lifecycle histories and preservation of native state in a non-git tracker."
  "2026-10-25T06:42:34.131Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed SDK calibrateObservedDurations and gantt calibrate, using complete-list certification, SDK current-item/history verification and SDK replay/patch primitives. Added explicit empirical scenario inputs. Evidence excludes whole reopened/canceled items, incomplete work, absent start estimates and unverified streams. Real public main 0586b6d: Task 25 selected/1 sample; Feature 17/0; Issue 42/1; Chore 27/1. Each refuses declared minimum 5; Task sample is 4.021616666666667 elapsed minutes vs 15 planned. Source copy remained unchanged without git available. Initial seeded model: 500 sequences, 2145 operations, 72 samples; repeated SDK item readback unchanged. Concurrency instrumentation now exercises 20 item/history read-boundary interleavings plus an unrelated-item revision change, preserving peer writes. Seven behavioral reverts were caught, including sample minimum, reopened/canceled exclusions, planned comparison, quantiles, revision validation and empirical sampling. No new import/sync/write journal or shared mutable state exists. Existing exporter is a schedule projection, not an item round trip. Full npm/Bun release gates will be measured in CI."
  "2026-10-25T06:44:38.398Z",codex-agent,"Local targeted verification passed: node --test test/calibration.test.ts test/uncertainty.test.ts test/smoke.test.ts reports 48 passed, 0 failed/skipped/canceled. Native SDK startTask/closeTask integration is included. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring and npm run duplication pass with unchanged thresholds; duplication is 0 percent. Seven behavioral revert probes fail with ERR_ASSERTION when the corresponding behavior is removed. The linked pm test command also passed; this tracker has result tracking disabled, so this comment retains the measured result instead of changing project policy. CI full npm/Bun release gates are pending."
  "2026-10-25T06:49:46.127Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40170241782 passed all 342 tests on Node 22.18.0 and Node 26, but correctly failed the unchanged 100 percent coverage gate: aggregate lines 99.95, branches 99.67, functions 100. The missing paths are the read-race exception handler and calibration command defaults/refusal in the in-process harness. Adding real foreign-write race coverage and command contract assertions. Public validation additionally passed with copied files/directories made read-only; counts and hashes remain identical. Isolated-home strict tracker health passes; normal-home health sees a globally installed pm-github host-version skew, not a tracked package change. Historical provenance advisory is inherited; no history repair or SDK pin change was made."
  "2026-10-25T06:50:39.038Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up verified locally: focused packed-command/default/refusal and real foreign item-write race tests pass (2 passed, 0 failed/skipped). The race corrupts a synthetic item after actual SDK history capture; calibration refuses without rewriting the foreign content and exercises the error handler. Read-only public tracker validation still reports the same 25/1, 17/0, 42/1 and 27/1 cohort/sample counts. Typecheck via build, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. Full coverage remains delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-25T06:51:42.818Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK review replaced local completion-field precedence with the SDK resolveCompletionTimestamp capability, supplying the verified closing transition timestamp as the legacy fallback. Focused duration comparison, exclusion and native lifecycle tests pass (3 tests); no estimate or state behavior changed. Waiting for CI coverage/release verification before final handoff."
  "2026-10-25T06:57:06.476Z",codex-agent,"CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/40170573836 passed for 77cfdd4: Node 22.18.0 coverage 343/343; Node 26 full npm release:check 343/343 and full Bun release:check 343/343; zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all six intended source files, unchanged thresholds. Build drift, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, audit, packed acceptance and changelog checks passed. Broader fleet overlap scan additionally found pm-rl chronological training-duration median thresholds and probability calibration diagnostics; those label/evaluate learned binary targets rather than compare start estimates or return observed scheduling populations. No duplicate scheduling feature was found. Seven revert probes and the read-only public corpus check were rerun successfully after adopting the SDK completion resolver. The PR body will retain the final exact-head CI receipt after this final SDK/evidence commit is reverified. External AI reviewers were skipped or quota-limited; no review approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-25T08:51:33.419Z",codex-agent,"Read-only review blocked PR 179: sparse empirical arrays bypass Array.every and can throw during date formatting. Reopened implementation work to centralize strict estimate, sampling and calibration input boundaries, reject holes/extra keys/nonfinite or out-of-range values before numerical work, fuzz public SDK/CLI/stored-field paths, and retain behavioral revert proof. Existing completed feature, real-data and state tests will be retained rather than repeated as new work."
  "2026-10-25T09:33:32.218Z",codex-agent,"Review class fix: duration-input.ts is the single declarative schema/interpreter (no validator dependency existed). Dense own-index arrays, finite range checks including negative zero rejection, closed option/estimate objects, dates, native effort fields, resource calendars/work overrides, repair inputs and supplied graphs now share it. Frozen detached values and module-owned receipts keep internal calculators from receiving unvalidated data; graph Maps become frozen entry arrays. Forecast CLI readers use SDK values directly, preserving native JSON negative zero. Deleted duplicated estimate/control validators. Seed 179202610: 2000 malformed cases across six SDK APIs plus two guarded adapters; 2000 CLI/native cases across six routes; no throws/writes. 300 valid generated scenarios retain pre-refactor digest 2e450ce71178de3816724bc7bbd1013843d3413d5e06b133b55e206bf3d8b346. Targeted 83-test run passed with schema coverage 100/100/100 before the final graph-specific checks; those additional four focused checks pass. Revert proof: node test/revert-duration-input.ts bypassed only empirical values validation; sparse regression failed with ERR_ASSERTION containing Invalid time value, and source was restored in finally. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and unchanged zero-duplication gate pass."
  "2026-10-25T09:37:03.514Z",codex-agent,"Final tracked fuzz command passed via pm test observed-duration --run --only-last --progress: 9 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations; 2000 SDK malformed cases and 2000 CLI/native cases at seed 179202610. Current source includes strict supplied-graph validation; graph-specific focused checks and immutable receipt/forgery checks pass. Legacy native civil timestamps and open SDK relationship metadata remain supported. Additional targeted forecast run passed 83 tests; new schema measured 100/100/100 in that targeted run. Final typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (17 files) and duplication (0 percent) pass. Empirical boundary revert reproduces the original Invalid time value assertion failure and restores the source. Existing calibration and uncertainty behavioral revert scripts were verified against the refactor. CI full unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release gates remain the final gate."
  "2026-10-25T09:42:04.912Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary hardening captures array length once from its own descriptor and validates that length through the same numeric rule, so proxy getters or changing length reads cannot alter the bounded index loop. The added focused regression passes without invoking a raw length getter; valid result digest, sparse cases and graph checks still pass. The empirical-boundary revert proof was repeated successfully and restored. Previous tracked 2000+2000-case fuzz evidence remains applicable; final CI re-runs the complete corpus at the pushed head."
  "2026-10-25T09:50:13.696Z",codex-agent,"Validation work is also capped at 1000000 schema steps and 10000 object fields; a shared-array product cannot bypass scalar/array bounds by aliasing. Supplied graphs capture intrinsic Map size and entry snapshots before child inspection, avoiding overridden size getters and live iterator growth. Focused regressions, valid-result digest, typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero duplication and the empirical revert proof pass. Final generated declaration maps are included with the built output. These are validation-boundary refinements only; scheduling arithmetic remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T10:06:42.629Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40182314920 executed 355 tests: 349 passed and 6 failed. The validator, calibration, resource and uncertainty modules reached 100/100/100; failures were an obsolete invalid_calibration regex plus legacy chart warning fixtures with estimates above the forecast ceiling. Shared schema now preserves the legacy renderer's finite nonnegative scalar contract while forecast/native-sampling estimates retain 0..175200 bounds. No forecast bound was widened. Pinned-host handler tests pass 42/42; focused packed calibration, valid digest and malformed historical-start tests pass 3/3. Added explicit prior-revision malformed effort and timestamp coverage. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero duplication and empirical-boundary revert proof pass. The strict read-only public-data validation still returns the original cohort/sample counts and identical hashes. Full gates are being rerun on the corrected head."
  "2026-10-25T10:20:45.029Z",codex-agent,"CI 40183449668 passed all 355 tests with no failures, but the unchanged coverage gate reported index.ts branch coverage 99.80 percent (aggregate 99.87). Added the real SDK missing-corpus resource command case with a valid scenarios file, covering the early read refusal independently of file validation. Focused regression passes; typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. New upstream release tag v2026.10.25 also made the generated changelog stale in CI; fetched tags and regenerated it with the existing package script, without changing package version or release policy. Changelog check passes. Full npm/Bun gates are rerunning; exact final receipt will be retained in the PR body."
  "2026-10-25T10:26:14.004Z",codex-agent,"CI 40184408310 exposed a merge-checkout changelog difference: upstream main had released v2026.10.25 and preserved source lifecycle/release metadata on synced issues. Integrated those upstream commits into the feature branch without editing their item/history pairs; the feature item is new and has no shared-main history. Regenerated changelog from the combined tracker; build, test typecheck, lint and changelog check pass. Isolated-home strict health passes, with inherited advisory provenance/telemetry findings only and no merge receipts pending. No release was created by this work. Full gates will rerun on the synchronized branch."
  "2026-10-25T10:31:18.216Z",codex-agent,"CI 40184785854 passed all 355 tests on both runtimes but retained one uncovered index.ts branch (99.90 percent; aggregate 99.93). Focused forecast coverage pinpointed line 3246: uncertainty command formatting of a semantic refusal after schema success. Added an SDK-backed non-git case with a well-formed point override for absent work; it asserts invalid_estimate, remedy/remediation, usage exit code and unchanged durable tracker hash. Focused packed CLI regression passes; build/test typecheck and lint pass. The strict schema itself remains measured at 100/100/100. This test-only follow-up leaves estimate and scheduling behavior unchanged; full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates rerun next."
  "2026-10-25T10:35:34.705Z",codex-agent,"Full CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/40185136546 passed on e095c03deba06d4fd00d641772d26b773ea4db21: Node 22.18.0 coverage 355/355, Node 26 npm run release:check 355/355, and Node 26 bun run release:check 355/355. Each reports zero failures, skips and cancellations; all seven intended source modules meet unchanged 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Tracker health, generated build, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, audit, real packed npm/Bun/minimum-host acceptance, changelog and release checks pass. CodeQL also passed. Seed 179202610 has 2000 malformed SDK plus 2000 CLI/native cases and the 300 valid-result digest remains identical. Empirical-boundary revert proof is recorded above. This final evidence-only commit will be reverified in CI; the PR body retains its exact-head receipt. Item remains open for orchestrator verification; no merge or release performed."
  "2026-10-25T14:15:48.250Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 review found finite start estimates can still overflow elapsed/planned ratios: 1e-308 planned minutes and 1440 elapsed minutes produces Infinity, serialized as null. Continuing the same item to define meaningful duration domains in the shared validator, check successful numeric/date output contracts, fuzz at least 2000 extreme cases including the exact report, and prove the output guard by behavioral revert. Existing strict input boundary and completed feature evidence remain intact."
  "2026-10-25T14:36:55.571Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 class fix in duration-input.ts: positive forecast estimates/elapsed observations are 1/60..175200 minutes, zero work remains explicit, and bounded legacy rendering allows at most 10512000 minutes (20 365-day years). Closed output schemas guard calibration, sampling, resources and repairs before SDK/CLI success; resource selection checks supplied output before any note mutation. Every numeric leaf is finite and ranged, numeric nulls refuse, ISO dates remain within four-digit years, and invalid_estimate names the output field with a remedy. Ratios are 0..10512000. PM-linked node --test test/duration-output.test.ts passed serially: 4/4, zero failures/skips/cancellations; seed 1792202610, 2000 cases, 341 accepted calibrations and 1659 refusals, six SDK and four CLI routes, SDK readback plus unchanged durable hashes. 398 output-field corruption probes passed. The exact 1e-308 planned / 1440 elapsed case refuses in SDK and packed JSON CLI. The initial 120-second PM run timed out and a run overlapping the temporary revert was discarded; the isolated serial run with 300-second budget passed in 264 seconds. Separate resource/uncertainty tests passed 45/45; 300 supported scenarios retain the original digest. Public read-only corpus counts remain Task 25/1, Feature 17/0, Issue 42/1, Chore 27/1 with unchanged hashes. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Revert proof: node test/revert-duration-output.ts removed only parse(outputSchemas[kind], value, kind); accepted SDK inputs emitted a year-10000 completion and the refusal assertion failed with ERR_ASSERTION. finally restored the source. CI full release gates pending."
  "2026-10-25T14:41:30.621Z",codex-agent,"CI 40203100080 measured 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all seven source modules; Node 22 passed 357/359 tests. The two failed legacy assertions expected now-unsupported behavior: an immediate native start/close under one second and a year-10000 repair baseline. Updated the actual SDK lifecycle fixture to wait 1100 milliseconds before close and assert the one-second floor; updated the repair fixture to assert invalid_estimate naming repair.baseline.finish. Both focused tests pass (2/2), with typecheck, test typecheck, lint and zero duplication passing. No production behavior or bounds changed in this follow-up. CI full npm/Bun gates rerun next."
  "2026-10-25T14:49:38.033Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 full CI passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/40203455014 on 3d3087e160f9aebd296a71ee3ad391e070359b3d. Node 22.18.0 coverage, Node 26 npm run release:check, and Node 26 bun run release:check each passed 359/359 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, with all seven intended source modules at unchanged 100 percent lines/branches/functions. CodeQL, tracker health, committed build, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, production audit, packed npm/Bun/minimum-host acceptance and changelog/release workflow checks pass. CI confirms seed 1792202610: 2000 cases, 341 accepted / 1659 refused calibrations, 398 output corruption probes, six SDK and four CLI routes, no durable writes. Exact tiny-estimate case and output-only revert proof are recorded above; public data counts remain unchanged. Final evidence-only commit will be reverified, and the PR body will retain its exact-head receipt. No merge or release performed; item stays open for orchestrator verification."
